Spec: Offset Tool

Purpose:
  Create parallel offset copies of paths at a specified distance.

Owns:
  ./offset.ts
  ./offset.test.ts

Must:
  Configurable distance in mm (positive = outward, negative = inward).
  Configurable join style: Round, Miter, Bevel.
  Hover preview shows green offset outline (cached, not recomputed every frame).
  Click applies the offset, replacing the original shape.
  Operation is fully undoable.

Must not:
  Recompute offset preview on every animation frame (use cache).
  Operate on open paths without warning.
  Crash on degenerate paths (catch Paper.js errors gracefully).

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @paper.js (for offset geometry)
  @OffsetCommand

Scenario: outward offset
  Given a 50mm square is on canvas and offset distance = 3mm
  When the user hovers over the square
  Then a green preview of a ~56mm square appears
  When the user clicks
  Then the original square is replaced by the offset result

Scenario: inward offset
  Given a 50mm square is on canvas and offset distance = -3mm
  When the user hovers over the square
  Then a green preview of a ~44mm square appears
  When the user clicks
  Then the original square is replaced by the inward offset result

Scenario: offset preview caching
  Given the Offset tool is active and the user hovers over a shape
  When the user moves the cursor slightly within the same shape
  Then the preview does not recompute (uses cached result)
  When the user changes the offset distance
  Then the preview recomputes with the new distance

Scenario: offset undo
  Given a shape has had an offset applied
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the original shape is restored

Scenario: offset on degenerate path
  Given a very small path where inward offset would self-intersect
  When the user hovers or clicks
  Then no crash occurs (error handled gracefully)
  And a notification may appear indicating the offset failed

Tasks:
  [x] Hover preview with caching.
  [x] Click to apply offset.
  [x] Distance and join configuration.
  [x] Error handling for degenerate paths.
  [x] Undoable via command.
